; PCP-I header template for the first AMD64 MiniOS optical image.
; This file contains only the ISO-9660/El Torito header sectors. It does not
; contain boot code, a filesystem, cursor data, or any other runtime payload.
;
; PADDING provides ISO LBAs 0..15 (the system area). The RAW image contains
; only LBAs 16..19: the primary descriptor, boot record, descriptor
; terminator, and the El Torito catalog header/default-entry hole.

MAGIC "pcpi"
VERSION 1
ENDIANNESS 1
BITORDER 1
SIGNATURE "MiniOS AMD64 ISO header only"
PADDING 32768

@RAW

; LBA 16: ISO-9660 primary volume descriptor.
01 43 44 30 30 31 01 00
ZERO 72
; Volume-space-size, filled after the final image layout is known.
[8]
ZERO 40
; Root-directory record/location metadata, filled by the ISO producer.
[32]
ZERO 1888

; LBA 17: El Torito boot-record descriptor.
00 43 44 30 30 31 01
45 4C 20 54 4F 52 49 54 4F 20 53 50 45 43 49 46 49 43 41 54 49 4F 4E 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20
52 49 46 20 4D 49 4E 49 4F 53 20 42 4F 4F 54 20 43 41 54 41 4C 4F 47 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20 20
; The catalog remains at LBA 19, so its El Torito pointer is static.
13
[16]
ZERO 1960

; LBA 18: volume-descriptor set terminator.
FF 43 44 30 30 31 01 00
ZERO 2040

; LBA 19: El Torito validation entry and default-entry hole.
01 00 52 49 46 20 4D 49 4E 49 4F 53 20 45 4C 54 4F 52 49 54 4F 20 43 41 54 20 00 00 00 00 55 AA
[16]
ZERO 2000
@END
